  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/1f3d0b514bc4ec701b6ac755b82cec7246a7a819400108e1733759eb0a2fec86.png)\n\nGiven the sets $A=\\{o,p,q,r\\}$ and $B=\\{q,r,v,w\\},$ find $A\\cup B.$",
  "worked_solution": "The union $A\\cup B$ consists of all the elements that are in either $A$ or $B,$ or both. To represent $A\\cup B,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in either $A$ or $B,$ or both.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14234521/assets/7984b0cb81df816388aa0d5cbf860fc4bdad9f7e871e8671d4616ded02bcaf5b.png)\n\nThe elements $o,p,q,r,v,w$ are in either $A$ or $B$, or both. Therefore, the union of $A$ and $B$ is\n\n$$\nA\\cup B=\\{o,p,q,r,v,w\\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
